<h3>About</h3>
<p>Released in 1991, this is the promo video for Enya single <a href="/watermark/#Exile">"Exile"</a>, from the album <a href="/watermark/"><em>Watermark</em></a>.</p>
<p>Time: 3:40</p>
<p>Directed by Michael Geoghegan.</p>

<p>"Exile" is a song by the Irish singer Enya. It was first released on her 1988 album Watermark, and was later released as the fourth and final single from the album in 1991 after it was featured in the film L.A. Story. The song also appeared in the 1995 film Cry, the Beloved Country and on the TV series Haven. German techno band Scooter sampled "Exile" on their single "Jigga Jigga!", taken from the 2004 album Mind the Gap. </p>

<p><strong><a href="/enya-video/">&laquo; EnyaTube home</a></strong></p>

</Layout>
